  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "  A singleton group can still contain multiple valid tokens. With x=[[1, 5]], group_size=1 and std_unbiased=False, this changes the output from approximately [-1, 1] to [-2, 2] by forcing std=1.\nCould we keep the remainder-slicing fix without broadening this shortcut？",
      "created_at": "2026-09-22T06:27:26Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -1607,8 +1614,8 @@ def __call__(\n                 group_mean_slice = mean[s]  # already computed and expanded\n                 group_sz = s.stop - s.start\n \n-                # Special case: with group_size=1 and std_unbiased=True, std should be 1 for numerical stability\n-                if group_sz == 1 and self.std_unbiased:\n+                # Special case: with group_size=1, std should be 1 for numerical stability\n+                if group_sz == 1:",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/areal-project/AReaL/pull/1673#discussion_r4068970786",
